From 7226b02399d5e65938946fbfc1bdb3ef8d71dc67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Kulke <magnuskulke@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 10:40:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wip: target/i386/mshv: deliver legacy PIC interrupts

MSHV provides an hypervisor-backed LAPIC, while QEMU owns the legacy PIC.

Once the PIC asserts an interrupt, we request an "interruption
deliverability" notification, so we get a dedicated exit once the
partition ready to accept it. We then inject the selected vector via a
"PendingEvent" register and resume a halted VP when necessary.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Kulke <magnuskulke@microsoft.com>
